+
\frac{e_o}{12}
+
\frac{e_o-16}{6}
=
0\] Multiplying throughout by \(12\), \[e_o-80+e_o+2(e_o-16)=0\] \[4e_o=112\] \[e_o=\frac{112}{4}=28~\text{V}\] Hence, the correct answer is \[\boxed{\textbf{D. }28~\text{V}}\]

The hybrid pi model of BJT is given as <img src="img/782464b70390b3e2.webp" loading="lazy" alt="" style="width:min(100%,288px)"> The small-signal collector current is \[i_{c}=g_{m}v_{\pi},\] where \[v_{\pi}=i_{b}r_{\pi}.\] \[\therefore i_{c}=g_{m}(i_{b}r_{\pi})
=g_{m}r_{\pi}i_{b}.\] Hence, the small-signal current gain is \[\beta=\frac{i_{c}}{i_{b}}
=g_{m}r_{\pi}.\] Hence the correct option is (C). \[\boxed{\text{(C)\quad}g_m r_\pi}\]

Given, \(g_{m}=38\,\text{mA/V}=0.038\,\text{S},
C_{\mu}=10^{-14}\,\text{F},
C_{\pi}=4\times10^{-13}\,\text{F} \text{ and }
\beta_{0}=90.\) The transition frequency is given by \[f_{T}=\frac{g_{m}}{2\pi(C_{\pi}+C_{\mu})}.\] \[f_{T}
=\frac{0.038}{2\pi(4\times10^{-13}+10^{-14})}
=1.47\times10^{10}\,\text{Hz}.\] The beta cut-off frequency is related to the transition frequency by \[f_{\beta}=\frac{f_{T}}{\beta_{0}}.\] Therefore, \[f_{\beta}
=\frac{1.47\times10^{10}}{90}
=1.64\times10^{8}\,\text{Hz}.\] Hence, the correct option is (B). \[\boxed{\text{(B)\quad $f_T = 1.47 \times 10^{10} Hz$ and $f_\beta = 1.64 \times 10^8 Hz$}}\]

Initially, all flags are <strong>RESET</strong> (\(\text{CY} = 0\), \(\text{Z} = 0\), \(\text{S} = 0\)). <ol><li><strong>FF00 H:</strong> MVI A, FFH \(\rightarrow\) Accumulator \(A = \text{FFH}\).</li><li><strong>FF02 H:</strong> INR A \(\rightarrow\) \(A = \text{FFH} + 01\text{H} = 00\text{H}\). Zero flag sets (\(\text{Z} = 1\)). Carry flag \(\text{CY}\) is unaffected by INR and remains \(0\).</li><li><strong>FF03 H:</strong> JC FF0CH \(\rightarrow\) Since \(\text{CY} = 0\), branch is <strong>not taken</strong>.</li><li><strong>FF06 H:</strong> ORI A8H \(\rightarrow\) \(A = 00\text{H} \lor \text{A8H} = \text{A8H}\). Logical operations clear carry (\(\text{CY} = 0\)). Sign flag sets (\(\text{S} = 1\)) because MSB is \(1\).</li><li><strong>FF08 H:</strong> JM FF15H \(\rightarrow\) Since \(\text{S} = 1\), branch to <strong>FF15 H</strong> is <strong>taken</strong>.</li><li><strong>FF15 H:</strong> MVI A, FFH \(\rightarrow\) \(A = \text{FFH}\).</li><li><strong>FF17 H:</strong> ADI 02H \(\rightarrow\) \(A = \text{FFH} + 02\text{H} = 01\text{H}\). Carry is generated (\(\text{CY} = 1\), \(\text{Z} = 0\)).</li><li><strong>FF19 H:</strong> RAL \(\rightarrow\) Rotate \(A\) left through carry. Initial \(A = 0000\,0001_2\), \(\text{CY} = 1\). After rotation, \(A = 0000\,0011_2 = 03\text{H}\) and \(\text{CY} = 0\) (MSB of \(A\) was \(0\)).</li><li><strong>FF1A H:</strong> JZ FF23H \(\rightarrow\) Since \(A = 03\text{H}\) (\(\text{Z} = 0\)), branch is <strong>not taken</strong>.</li><li><strong>FF1D H:</strong> JC FF10H \(\rightarrow\) Since \(\text{CY} = 0\), branch is <strong>not taken</strong>.</li><li><strong>FF20 H:</strong> JNC FF12H \(\rightarrow\) Since \(\text{CY} = 0\), branch to <strong>FF12 H</strong> is <strong>taken</strong>.</li><li><strong>FF12 H:</strong> OUT PORT 2 \(\rightarrow\) \(03\text{H}\) is written to <strong>PORT 2</strong>.</li><li><strong>FF14 H:</strong> HLT \(\rightarrow\) Execution halts.</li></ol> \[\boxed{\begin{aligned}
    \text{MVI A, FFH} &amp;\rightarrow \text{INR A} \rightarrow \text{JC FF0CH} \rightarrow \text{ORI A8H} \rightarrow \text{JM FF15H} \rightarrow \text{MVI A, FFH} \\
    &amp;\rightarrow \text{ADI 02H} \rightarrow \text{RAL} \rightarrow \text{JZ FF23H} \rightarrow \text{JC FF10H} \rightarrow \text{JNC FF12H} \\
    &amp;\rightarrow \text{OUT PORT 2} \rightarrow \text{HLT}
    \end{aligned}}\] <div class="sol-block sol-keypoints"><div class="sol-block-title">Key points</div><ul><li>The INR instruction does not alter the Carry flag.</li><li>Logical instructions (ORI, XRA, etc.) always clear the Carry flag.</li></ul></div>

Given : \(G(s) = \dfrac{k(s - 2)}{(s + 2)^2}\ \ and\ \ H(s) = s - 2\). The closed-loop characteristic equation is given by \(1 + G(s)H(s) = 0\): \[1 + k \frac{(s - 2)}{(s + 2)^2} (s - 2) = 0 \implies (k + 1)s^2 + (4 - 4k)s + (4 + 4k) = 0\] RH Table: \[\begin{array}{c|cc}
s^2 &amp; k + 1 &amp; 4 + 4k \\
s^1 &amp; 4 - 4k &amp; 0 \\
s^0 &amp; 4 + 4k &amp; 
\end{array}\] For stability, all elements in the first column must be strictly positive: <ul><li>From \(s^1\) row: \(4 - 4k &gt; 0 \implies k &lt; 1\)</li><li>From \(s^0\) row: \(4 + 4k &gt; 0 \implies k &gt; -1\)</li></ul> Given the physical constraint \(k \ge 0\), the valid range for stability is: \[\boxed{(C) \ only \ if\ \ 0 \le k &lt; 1 }\]

